INT. ASSEMBLY ROOM, BATH - 1790s - NIGHT

Candles. A string quartet. Powdered wigs. Silk and sweat.

LADY CONSTANCE ASHWORTH-BELLAMY (30s) and MISS GEORGIANA TREVELYAN-SOLOMON (20s) stand at the edge of the dance floor, fans snapping. A third woman, DUCHESS ELEANOR MARCHMONT-IDOWU (60s), leans heavily on her cane between them.

CONSTANCE
She's staring again.

GEORGIANA
Who?

CONSTANCE
The Duchess. She thinks we cannot see her.

DUCHESS
I can hear you perfectly well.

GEORGIANA
Your Grace --

DUCHESS
Do not "Your Grace" me. You were both whispering.

CONSTANCE
We were admiring your pearls.

DUCHESS
You were admiring my debts.

GEORGIANA
Never!

DUCHESS
Then you are fools. Everyone else is.

The quartet begins a minuet. The Duchess lifts her cane and points it at the floor.

DUCHESS (CONT'D)
Dance, both of you. And smile.
